ark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/whir.rs`\n\n**High-level flow:**\n```\nprove_whir_opening_gpu()\n├─ Pre-WHIR Setup (lines 74-178):\n│  ├─ whir_algebraic_batch_traces() — Batch all matrices via mu powers (18ms)\n│  ├─ batch_ntt_small() — iDFT on chunks of size 2^l_skip \n│  ├─ transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec() — Convert F base-field to EF extended-field\n│  └─ mle_interpolate_stage_ext() [l_skip iterations] — Zeta transform (stages 0..l_skip)\n│\n└─ WHIR Rounds (lines 199-515):\n   for whir_round in 0..num_whir_rounds {\n      for round in 0..k_whir {  // k_whir sumcheck rounds per WHIR round\n         ├─ whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round() — Compute s(X) for X in {1,2} (3ms per call, 80 instances)\n         ├─ [Grind for alpha] — Transcript interaction\n         └─ whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments() — Fold f and w polynomials (3ms per call, 80 instances)\n      }\n      ├─ split_ext_to_base_col_major_matrix() — Convert EF → F\n      ├─ batch_expand_pad() + batch_ntt() — RS codeword generation\n      ├─ MerkleTreeGpu::new_with_hash() — Merkle tree commitment\n      ├─ eval_poly_ext_at_point_from_base() — OOD evaluation\n      ├─ [Query phase] — Sample indices\n      ├─ batch_query_merkle_proofs() — Get merkle proofs\n      └─ w_moments_accumulate() — Update moment vector (7ms per call, 14 instances)\n   }\n```\n\n### 2. Data Flow and Dependencies\n\n**Before WHIR Rounds:**\n- `stacked_per_commit` contains multiple AIR commitments (common main + preprocessed + cached traces)\n- Each has its own unstacked traces (stored as `DeviceMatrix<F>`)\n\n**Algebraic Batching (Line 128):**\n- Kernel: `whir_algebraic_batch_traces_kernel` (18ms, 6 instances)\n- Input: One trace packet per trace in all commitments\n- Output: Single batched `f_ple_evals` vector (height × D_EF elements, combining all AIRs)\n- Uses packets to index into multiple trace buffers simultaneously\n- Applies mu powers algebraically within the kernel\n\n**Coefficient Computation:**\n- `batch_ntt_small()` does in-place iDFT on chunks (height × D_EF elements)\n- `transpose_fp_to_fpext_vec()` converts to EF form\n- `mle_interpolate_stage_ext()` runs l_skip times (zeta transform)\n\n**Per WHIR Round:**\n- Operates on `f_coeffs` (height × EF) and `w_moments` (height × EF)\n- Size halves after each k_whir group of sumcheck rounds\n- `f_coeffs` and `w_moments` are maintained in coefficient/moment form (not evaluation form)\n\n### 3. Stacked Reduction Interaction\n\n**Connection Point:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs:166-184`\n\n```rust\nlet (stacking_proof, u_prisma, stacked_per_commit) = \n    prove_stacked_opening_reduction_gpu();  // Returns Vec<StackedPcsData2>\n\nlet whir_proof = prove_whir_opening_gpu(..., stacked_per_commit, &u_cube)?;\n```\n\n**Data Handoff:**\n- Stacked Reduction outputs `StackedPcsData2` structs (defined in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs:121`)\n- Each contains:\n  - `inner: Arc<StackedPcsDataGpu>` — PCS data (Merkle tree of stacked matrix)\n  - `traces: Vec<DeviceMatrix<F>>` — Unstacked traces in prismalinear form\n  \n**WHIR receives:** `Vec<StackedPcsData2>` where each element is one commitment (common main, preprocessed, or cached)\n\n**Height consistency:** All commitments must have the same stacked height (verified at line 81-84)\n\n**Width aggregation:** Total width across all commitments = sum of individual widths (line 118, line 147 in gpu_backend.rs)\n\n### 4. Parallelism Opportunities\n\n**Current Bottleneck: Sequential Within-Round Execution**\n\nThe nested loop structure (whir_round → k_whir rounds) is fully sequential:\n- Each sumcheck round waits for fold to complete\n- Each fold requires s_evals from transcript interaction\n- No explicit CUDA streams used for multi-kernel overlap\n\n**Potential Multi-Stream Opportunities:**\n\n**A. Cross-Segment Kernel Dispatch (Within Single WHIR Round):**\n- `whir_algebraic_batch_traces()` processes one batch at a time\n- Could partition stacked_per_commit by AIR and dispatch 6+ kernel launches to different streams\n- Current: 18ms single batch\n- Potential: Launch per-AIR batches in parallel if independent\n\n**B. Merkle Tree Operations (Per-Round, Round > 0):**\n- Lines 371-464: Query phase happens after folding\n- `batch_query_merkle_proofs()` (one tree) and `batch_open_rows()` could use multiple streams\n- Limited by data dependencies on query_indices (sampled sequentially)\n\n**C. NTT Batch Expansion Pipelining:**\n- Lines 299-315: `batch_expand_pad()` + `batch_ntt()` are sequential\n- Both operate on D_EF independent polynomials\n- Could overlap expand and NTT launches on different stream queues\n\n**D. w_moments_accumulate Parallelization:**\n- Line 501: Currently single kernel call per WHIR round\n- Works element-wise on w_moments buffer\n- 14 instances suggests this is already batched/tuned\n\n**E. Cross-WHIR-Round Blocking:**\n- Fundamental dependency: Each round's sumcheck requires alpha from previous round's fold\n- NO opportunity to parallelize across whir_rounds due to transcript dependencies\n- But within each whir_round, can parallelize k_whir sumcheck+fold pairs if alpha batching worked\n\n**F. Segment-Aware Batching (Most Promising):**\nEach AIR has its own trace (lines 105-119 construct separate packets per AIR):\n```rust\nfor stacked in &stacked_per_commit {\n    for (trace, &idx) in zip(&stacked.traces, &layout.mat_starts) {\n        packets.push(BatchingTracePacket { ... });\n    }\n}\n```\n- Could launch separate `whir_algebraic_batch_traces` for each trace into different streams\n- Reduces synchronization overhead for per-AIR dispatch\n- Would require careful D2H copy of mu_powers (currently shared)\n\n### 5. Scaling Properties\n\n**WHIR Scales with:**\n- **AIR Count (Commits):** YES - algebraic batch traces kernel processes all packets in single kernel, but num_packets parameter shows per-AIR dispatch point\n- **Total Data Volume:** YES - height/width of stacked matrix drives f_coeffs and w_moments size; w_moments_accumulate runs over full height\n\n**Size-Sensitive Components:**\n- `whir_algebraic_batch_traces`: O(stacked_height) work, parallelizes over rows/packets\n- `whir_sumcheck_coeff_moments_round`: O(height) threads, block-reduces, then static 2-reduction (S_DEG=2)\n- `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments`: O(height/2) threads, element-wise operation\n- `batch_expand_pad` + `batch_ntt`: O(D_EF × codeword_height) for each round\n\n**NOT Scaling Features:**\n- Merkle tree operations (only initial round uses stacked_per_commit; subsequent rounds use single g_tree)\n- num_whir_rounds = (m - log_final_poly_len) / k_whir — Fixed by parameters\n- Query phase: num_queries is constant per round\n\n### 6. Key Insights for 176ms → Faster Path\n\nCurrent split: WHIR (101ms) + Stacked Reduction (74ms) = 175ms\n\n**Quick wins in WHIR kernel launch overhead:**\n1. **Batch heterogeneous AIR traces separately** instead of merged packet array (6 instances vs 1)\n2. **Kernel fusion candidates:**\n   - `whir_fold_coeffs_and_moments` + next round's `whir_sumcheck` input pre-load\n   - `batch_expand_pad` + immediate `batch_ntt` (they're sequential, could fuse)\n3. **Reduce temporary buffer allocations** in sumcheck loop (line 214-216 reallocates if capacity insufficient)\n\n**Stacked Reduction interaction:**\n- Only first WHIR round touches stacked_per_commit (line 375-442)\n- Traces cleared after first round if backing matrix cached (line 131-135)\n- Second+ rounds use only single RS tree: efficient\n\n---\n\n**Files for deeper investigation:**\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/whir.cu` — Kernel implementations\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` — Stacked reduction kernels\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/ntt.rs` — Batch NTT wrapper"}],"totalDurationMs":45929,"totalTokens":51845,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_token