aces → rs_code_matrix → merkle_tree)\n\n**Stacking Groups Handling (lines 134-173):**\n```rust\nfor (mat_idx, j, s) in &layout.sorted_cols {\n    let descs: Vec<StackColDesc> = Vec::with_capacity(layout.sorted_cols.len());\n    // ... build descriptor array on HOST (CPU-only, no CUDA API calls)\n}\n// Phase 2: Upload descriptors to GPU and launch SINGLE scatter kernel\nif !descs.is_empty() {\n    let d_descs = descs.to_device()?;\n    unsafe { stack_columns(&d_descs).map_err(...)? };  // One kernel call\n}\n```\n\n**Result:** All stacking groups are processed in a **single `stack_columns_kernel` launch** with one block per column descriptor.\n\n---\n\n### 5. DATA FLOW: STACKING → HASHING → MERKLE TREE\n\n```\nTrace Matrices (multiple AIRs, different heights)\n  ↓\n[stack_traces_into_expanded()]\n  ├─ Allocate stacked matrix buffer (width × height)\n  ├─ Build StackColDesc array on CPU\n  └─ Launch stack_columns_kernel (1 block per descriptor)\n  ↓\nStacked Matrix (mixed form: h=2^(l_skip+n_stack), w=sum of trace widths)\n  ↓\n[rs_code_matrix()]\n  ├─ batch_expand_pad: h × w → (h << log_blowup) × w\n  ├─ batch_ntt_small: iNTT on chunks of size 2^l_skip\n  ├─ mle_interpolate_stages: l_skip stages of coeffs→evals\n  ├─ bit_rev: prepare for NTT\n  └─ batch_ntt: DFT on smoothly-embedded domain\n  ↓\nRS Codeword Matrix (height << log_blowup, width)\n  ↓\n[MerkleTreeGpu::new_generic_with_hash<MH>()]\n  ├─ compress_rows() → poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel\n  │  └─ Output: query_digest_layer (height / rows_per_query digests)\n  ├─ While num_layers > 1:\n  │  └─ compress_layer() → poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel\n  │     (layer_by_layer, sequentially)\n  └─ Copy root from GPU to host\n  ↓\nMerkle Root (trace commitment) + Tree layers (cached on GPU)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. SYNCHRONIZATION POINTS\n\n**Explicit synchronization barriers (blocking H2D/D2H or kernel dependencies):**\n\n1. **After `stack_columns_kernel`** (implicit via DeviceBuffer operations)\n   - `stack_traces_into_expanded()` returns → all stacking complete\n\n2. **After `batch_expand_pad()` → before `batch_ntt_small()`**\n   - RS codeword matrix expansion must complete before iNTT\n\n3. **After each merkle layer compression**\n   - Merkle tree construction loops: `while digest_layers.last().unwrap().len() > 1`\n   - Each `compress_layer()` reads output of previous layer (sync point)\n   - Loop line 143-160 in merkle_tree.rs\n\n4. **After final layer → root copy D2H**\n   - `let root = d_root.to_host()?.pop().unwrap();` (line 163, merkle_tree.rs)\n   - D2H transfer blocks CPU until complete\n\n**Implicit synchronization:**\n- CUDA default stream serializes all kernels\n- No concurrent kernel execution between phases\n\n---\n\n### 7. OPTIMIZATION OPPORTUNITIES\n\n#### **A. `poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel` Batching (457 instances)**\n\n**Current Issue:**\n- Each layer compression launches a separate kernel (64 instances per layer, ~8 layers)\n- Kernel launch overhead: ~5-10μs per launch\n- Individual kernel runtime: ~26μs per launch\n- **Overhead ratio: 16-33% of execution time**\n\n**Optimization Strategy:**\n```cuda\n// BEFORE: 64 separate kernel launches for layer 1\ncompress_layer(layer1_output, layer0, layer0.len()/2)  // kernel launch 1\ncompress_layer(layer2_output, layer1, layer1.len()/2)  // kernel launch 2\n...  // 62 more launches\n\n// AFTER: Fused kernel processing all layers\nfused_merkle_layers_kernel(\n  output_ptrs[],     // pointers to all output layers\n  input_ptr,         // pointer to leaf layer\n  layer_sizes[],     // size of each layer\n  num_layers\n)\n// Single kernel launch with grid.y = num_layers\n```\n\n**Expected Gain:**\n- Eliminate 63 kernel launches × 7-10μs = **441-630 μs overhead recovery**\n- **Current:** 12ms for 457 instances\n- **Potential:** 11.5-11.6ms (1-4% improvement, but reduces CPU-GPU round-trip)\n\n#### **B. `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` Optimization**\n\n**Current Bottleneck Analysis:**\n-