tion:**\n```rust\nprover_config: GpuProverConfig {\n    cache_stacked_matrix: false,      // Save memory, recompute in reduction\n    cache_rs_code_matrix: true,       // Cache RS codes (performance > memory)\n    zerocheck_save_memory: true,      // Only for log_blowup == 1\n}\n```\n\n**Opportunity:** Empirically test `cache_stacked_matrix = true` for latency-critical paths (production mode)\n- Trade: ~(height × width × sizeof(F)) bytes for elimination of recomputation during stacked reduction\n- Height = 2^(l_skip + n_stack), Width = total AIR widths\n- At APC 300: ~100M elements × 4 bytes = 400 MB (often acceptable on modern GPUs)\n\n---\n\n### 8. KEY FINDINGS SUMMARY\n\n| Component | Time | Instances | Optimization Priority |\n|-----------|------|-----------|----------------------|\n| `poseidon2_compressing_row_hashes_kernel` | 231ms | 25 | **HIGH** - row hashing is dominant |\n| `poseidon2_strided_compress_layer_kernel` | 12ms | 457 | **MEDIUM** - kernel launch overhead |\n| `calculate_zero_hash` (zerocheck MLE) | 110ms | 584 | Not Trace Commit (different phase) |\n| `merkle_tree_init` (leaves creation) | 71ms | 2 | Part of compress_rows |\n| `merkle_tree_compress` (layers) | 75ms | 64 | Included in strided_compress total |\n| `stack_columns_kernel` | 16ms | 11 | **LOW** - already efficient |\n\n**Critical Path:**\n1. Stack traces (16ms) - fast\n2. RS code matrix (not separately profiled, part of merkle time)\n3. Row hashing (231ms) - **bottleneck**\n4. Layer compression (87ms) - secondary bottleneck\n\n**Total Trace Commit: ~246ms** at APC 300 (as stated)\n\n---\n\n### 9. FILE PATH REFERENCE\n\n**Core Implementation Files:**\n\n| File | Lines | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` | 48-84, 117-173, 182-279 | Trace commit orchestration, stacking, RS coding |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/gpu_backend.rs` | 55-74 | GPU backend `TraceCommitter` implementation |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/merkle_tree.rs` | 52-161 | Merkle tree construction (generic) |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/merkle_tree.cu` | 16-79, 153-177, 185-210 | Poseidon2 hashing and merkle kernels |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/matrix.cu` | 232-385 | Stack columns kernel |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/merkle_tree.rs` | 1-161 | FFI wrappers for CUDA kernels |\n| `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/device.rs` | 1-66 | GPU device configuration (`GpuProverConfig`) |\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive analysis provides the complete call chain, detailed kernel behaviors, data flow, synchronization points, and concrete optimization opportunities for the Trace Commit path of the CUDA-accelerated STARK prover."}],"totalDurationMs":102256,"totalTokens":68275,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1259,"cache_read_input_tokens":61354,"output_tokens":5658,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1259},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":5658,"cache_read_input_tokens":61354,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1259,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":8,"bashCount":16,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
