vement, which is pretty similar to the Round 0 precompute option at 1.63x and the MLE per-trace overhead approach at 1.61x. The Round 0 precompute actually edges ahead because it saves less at APC 0, which helps the ratio. Now I'm wondering if there's a way to apply multi-streaming directly to the stacked reduction code itself.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2849,"cache_read_input_tokens":169147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2849},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c275100b-138e-43b1-b6e9-07f6d601a462","uuid":"aa1e2d8f-0a74-4bcc-8738-b16176cf6c91"}
