{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011nvtg9sCAX3oG9kGZRbZ79","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SettDXsospFMhnRiDJ4Fyx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0\n\nMulti-stream the per-trace sequential loops in Stacked Reduction's Round 0 sumcheck (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`) and PLE fold (`fold_ple_evals`). These two functions currently launch ~797 sequential per-trace CUDA kernels on the default stream (22ms + 18ms GPU time, ~57ms wall time including launch overhead). Distributing across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams — the same pattern that improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~7ms wall time, saving ~50ms at APC 300.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":190907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c275100b-138e-43b1-b6e9-07f6d601a462","uuid":"c670b4bf-805c-4052-ba69-43490216bf71"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SettDXsospFMhnRiDJ4Fyx","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c275100b-138e-43b1-b6e9-07f6d601a462","uuid":"59cd01f7-4800-4f93-aa71-4799313fa8af","timestamp":"2026-04-14T00:03:20.358Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0\n\nMulti-stream the per-trace sequential loops in Stacked Reduction's Round 0 sumcheck (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`) and PLE fold (`fold_ple_evals`). These two functions currently launch ~797 sequential per-trace CUDA kernels on the default stream (22ms + 18ms GPU time, ~57ms wall time including launch overhead). Distributing across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams — the same pattern that improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~7ms wall time, saving ~50ms at APC 300.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid","+# 2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0"," ","-Right-size the GKR input evaluation kernel grid for small GLOBAL-mode AIRs. Currently, the CUDA launcher always uses `TASK_SIZE=65536` as the thread count for GLOBAL mode, launching 256 blocks regardless of the AIR's actual height. For the majority of AIRs at APC 300 (height << 65536), over 98% of threads exit immediately at the boundary check, yet each 256-block kernel saturates the RTX 4090's 128 SMs, preventing concurrent execution across the 8 multi-stream worker threads. Changing the launcher to use `min(TASK_SIZE, height)` allows small-AIR kernels to use proportionally fewer blocks (e.g., 4 blocks for height=1024 instead of 256), freeing SMs for concurrent kernel execution from other threads. This should dramatically improve multi-stream concurrency in GKR input eval — the single largest sub-component at APC 300 (seg0: 241ms, 17.6% of STARK excl trace).","+Multi-stream the per-trace sequential loops in Stacked Reduction's Round 0 sumcheck (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`) and PLE fold (`fold_ple_evals`). These two functions currently launch ~797 sequential per-trace CUDA kernels on the default stream (22ms + 18ms GPU time, ~57ms wall time including launch overhead). Distributing across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams — the same pattern that improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~7ms wall time, saving ~50ms at APC 300."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-0030-rightsize-gkr-input-kernel-grid\n\nRight-size the GKR input evaluation kernel grid for small GLOBAL-mode AIRs. Currently, the CUDA launcher always uses `TASK_SIZE=65536` as the thread count for GLOBAL mode, launching 256 blocks regardless of the AIR's actual height. For the majority of AIRs at APC 300 (height << 65536), over 98% of threads exit immediately at the boundary check, yet each 256-block kernel saturates the RTX 4090's 128 SMs, preventing concurrent execution across the 8 multi-stream worker threads. Changing the launcher to use `min(TASK_SIZE, height)` allows small-AIR kernels to use proportionally fewer blocks (e.g., 4 blocks for height=1024 instead of 256), freeing SMs for concurrent kernel execution from other threads. This should dramatically improve multi-stream concurrency in GKR input eval — the single largest sub-component at APC 300 (seg0: 241ms, 17.6% of STARK excl trace).\n"}}
