{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W5cYZN1gwzBersqXuyoWsV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0140-multistream-stacked-reduction-round0\n2\t\n3\tMulti-stream the per-trace sequential loops in Stacked Reduction's Round 0 sumcheck (`batch_sumcheck_uni_round0_poly`) and PLE fold (`fold_ple_evals`). These two functions currently launch ~797 sequential per-trace CUDA kernels on the default stream (22ms + 18ms GPU time, ~57ms wall time including launch overhead). Distributing across 8 OS threads with per-thread CUDA streams — the same pattern that improved Round 0 by 1.89x and GKR input eval by 1.40x — should reduce this to ~7ms wall time, saving ~50ms at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQEqiStJ2LoK9HRLx2iMQU","session_id":"c275100b-138e-43b1-b6e9-07f6d601a462","uuid":"a21a4c50-3ef7-4a24-9c9b-58b7d9c45fba","timestamp":"2026-04-14T00:04:54.895Z"}
